=== SURVEY ===
DB columns for notification_channels: id, name, kind, enabled, created_at, updated_at
No 'config' column — config lives in per-kind child tables (notification_channel_discord, etc.)
No 'type' column — renamed to 'kind' in db-refactor migration.

Code had:
  - SQL references to column 'type' (should be 'kind')
  - SQL references to column 'config' (does not exist — removed from schema)
  - json.Marshal/Unmarshal of config JSONB (no longer needed)

NotificationChannel model at internal/models/models.go:391
  - Type field db tag was "type", needs "kind"
  - Config field db tag was "config", needs "-" (not a DB column)

ch.Type used in 50+ places across handlers/workers/automation — renaming Go field out of scope.

=== REASONING ===
Keep Go field name 'Type' (avoid cascading changes across dozens of files).
Change only db tag: db:"type" → db:"kind".
Mark Config: db:"-" since it's not a DB column.
Fix 4 SQL queries in notification_repo.go: type→kind, remove config column.
Remove json.Marshal/Unmarshal of cfgJSON (no config column to read/write).
Remove unused imports (encoding/json, fmt).
Initialize Config to empty map on reads so callers don't hit nil map.

